  "task": "CONTEXT. ES-1G is Track D's Einstein-Straus benchmark: a black hole of mass M = 1 in a vacuum bubble inside expanding dust, wall at 36 M, outer dust edge at 60 M (data run D-20261115-170213-d2c2131). It was evolved at M/8 for 200 M with core's lapse_leak = 0.5 (T = 2 M) in place of plain 1+log, using the card executable /data/haiyangw/nrpic/scratch/core/exe/core_gauge/athena_gpu. The run is D-20261119-142633-6f72922 (Slurm 4636). It ran unattended on 2026-11-19 from 07:36 to 08:24 PST, and `scripts/submit_chain.sh --status` reports DONE (tlim), cycle 6400. The session that submitted it was cut off by the usage limit, so the manifest still says 'submitted', 0.98 card-hours are still reserved, and nothing has been analysed. The predictions G1-G7 were written before submission in tracks/D-bh-dress/es_runs/JOURNAL.md entry 5. The comparison runs are ES-1 (D-20261115-172726-60ba4c2, plain 1+log) and V-1 (D-20261115-172730-c6d151b, the same slice without dust). Your directory is tracks/D-bh-dress/es_runs/, which already exists: continue its JOURNAL.md with entry 9.\n\nREAD FIRST:\n- es_runs/README.md.\n- es_runs/JOURNAL.md entries 4 to 8 and the closing 'State' section (lines 213-557).\n- es_runs/tools/finish_es1g.sh and es_runs/tools/es_extra.py.\n- /data/haiyangw/nrpic/scratch/core/exe/core_gauge/READY: option 1 and test 'ES', which is core's own 30 M run on these data, core-20261115-202901-b4430da.\n- tracks/D-bh-dress/flux_tools/README.md, section 'Results', the ES-1/V-1 item. It found that the code's particle energy E = alpha W - beta^i u_i is not the Killing energy in this gauge.\n\nDO, IN ORDER (check the pause flag /data/haiyangw/nrpic/locks/PAUSE before each step):\n1. Confirm the chain says DONE. Open journal entry 9 with what you are about to do. Entry 5 stands unchanged. Its known flaw, recorded in entry 6 item E3, is that group R0 = 40 M lies in the inner dust edge: judge G1-G3 on group R0 = 48 M and report R0 = 40 M separately.\n2. From the worktree root, run tracks/D-bh-dress/es_runs/tools/finish_es1g.sh. It closes the run with nrpic-run finish, registers es_extra.py on ES-1, V-1 and ES-1G, and copies the results to results/es_extra_es1g.json and the figures to figs/es1g/. If the script fails, fix it inside es_runs/tools/ and record the fix. Then run `harness/bin/nrpic-run verify D-20261119-142633-6f72922`; it takes minutes for outputs of this size.\n3. Look at every PNG in figs/es1g/ with the Read tool.\n   - Judge each of G1 to G7 exactly as written: held, failed or not judgeable, with the number and the run id.\n   - Record every gauge pathology entry 5 lists: a start-up pulse of the relaxation; a lapse below 1 inside the dust; a front from the dust edges reaching the hole; the mesh minimum of the lapse near the hole against alpha_exc = 0.05 (column 16 of <base>.nrpic.hst; risk R14).\n   - Measure, without a prediction, whether the common late horizon drift of ES-1 and V-1 after t ~ 165 M appears in ES-1G. Use t0 = 100 M and give the drifts over the windows 100-165 M and 100-200 M. If you need a further measurement, register it (nrpic-run submit --package tracks/D-bh-dress/es_runs) and write its prediction first.\n4. Compare with core's own ES test in core_gauge/READY on the overlap 0-30 M: horizon mass 0.99997 at t = 10 M, drift 1.0e-3 to 30 M, lapse in the dust 1.04-1.06, largest lapse 1.11.\n5. Find every place where es_runs/analyse.py and tools/es_extra.py use the code's particle energy E. For each reported number, state whether it depends on E.\n6. Add a README section 'Gauge for the null test with matter'. On the evidence of ES-1, V-1 and ES-1G, say which lapse condition the G2 vacuum-bubble and matter runs should use, labelled [JUDGEMENT], with the numbers it rests on, and say what is still missing for the null-test floor. Do not state the floor itself: the late-drift controls run in parallel in package drift_controls.\n7. Update README.md: the run table, the ES-1G results with run ids, and the figures. Commit path-limited: git add tracks/D-bh-dress/es_runs tracks/D-bh-dress/runs, then git commit -m '...' -- tracks/D-bh-dress/es_runs tracks/D-bh-dress/runs.\n\nLIMITS: card time 0 (no new simulation). Analysis only, at most 4 cores.\n\nTRAPS:\n- trajmet records hold 17 doubles; proper time is index 12.\n- The finder writes <base>.horizon_summary_0.txt into the working directory.\n- A run that went non-finite still ends 'successfully', with zero particles: check column 3 of <base>.nrpic.hst.\n- Tracers carry m = 1e-30.\n- psi = 1 outside the ball: read masses as horizon or Misner-Sharp masses, never from the 1/r tail.\n- Never kill by pattern. Never rm through a path built from a shell variable.\n\nDONE WHEN: the run is finished and verified; entry 9 gives the outcome of every prediction G1-G7 with numbers and run ids; every figure in figs/es1g/ has been looked at and is described in the journal; README has the ES-1G results and the gauge judgement; everything is committed.",
