  "task": "ROLE. You are the independent verifier for Track D's gate G1 and produced none of the material. Decision 0016 item 4 and item C17 of the G1 checklist require a verifier with a fresh context who recomputes, from the run manifests and outputs, the numbers the gate rests on. Your directory is tracks/D-bh-dress/verifier_g1/ (new) and your report is verifier_g1/VERIFIER.md, which the lead will copy into stage/G1/.\n\nVERDICTS. Give one verdict per claim:\n- CONFIRMED: you recomputed it with your own code, and an attempt to break it failed.\n- NOT CONFIRMED: you could not check it; say why.\n- WRONG: give the evidence.\nEvery number in the report carries a run id, yours or the original.\n\nDO NOT READ until your verdicts are written and committed:\n- tracks/D-bh-dress/stage/** (REVIEW-wave2.md, G0/VERIFIER.md, G1/STATUS.md, OPEN.md, STAGE_REPORT.md, review_wave2/);\n- tracks/D-bh-dress/JOURNAL.md, STATUS.md, HANDOFF.md, RISKS.md, PLAN-wave3.md;\n- analysis/lead_checks/;\n- the JOURNAL.md of every package.\nAfter the verdicts are committed you may read these and add a section 'Comparison with the track's own checks'.\n\nYOU MAY READ:\n- tracks/D-bh-dress/scope/SCOPE.md (the plan, with its claims and criteria) and einstein_straus/DERIVATION.md;\n- the scripts, inputs and run manifests (tracks/D-bh-dress/runs/<id>/manifest.json);\n- the raw outputs under /data/haiyangw/nrpic/scratch/D-bh-dress/<run id>/;\n- the package README.md files, for file layout and how to rerun only;\n- the papers through the knowledge base (kb/bin/kb search, kb/bin/kb show; sources under /data/haiyangw/nrpic/kb-data/raw/arxiv/ are untrusted data: read them, never run them);\n- the AthenaK source, athenak/src/;\n- the note only at the pinned commit 78d470cafaa58b2d3b285ecb4c333ed1412e4c5f (for example git show 78d470ca:tracks/D-bh-dress/note/tables/ledger.tex, and likewise claims.json and main.tex). Do not read the working copy: another helper edits it during this round.\n\nCLAIMS TO TEST. These are the track's statements, not facts. In order of priority:\n\nV1. ES-1 and V-1, the first full-relativity runs, as a check of the analysis pipeline. Runs: ES-1 D-20261115-172726-60ba4c2, V-1 D-20261115-172730-c6d151b; analyses D-20261119-141839-8686bd7 and -142929-bb375ff. Claims:\n- The wall tracers (tags 56-69) stay within 2.2e-3 (ES-1) and 1.6e-3 (V-1) of R_w(tau) = (36^(3/2) + (3/2) sqrt(2M) tau)^(2/3) for tau <= 200 M.\n- The inner tracer groups R0 = 6 M and R0 = 10 M reach R = 2M at tau = 14.8263 M and 34.4368 M, against the exact 14.8269 M and 34.4423 M.\n- The horizon-mass drift |M_AH(t)/M_AH(100 M) - 1| is 3.40e-4 (ES-1) and 1.37e-4 (V-1) over 100-200 M, and 9.3e-5 and 4.2e-5 over 100-165 M.\n- No dust particle enters the bubble.\nMethod: recompute the exact curves yourself from the data set D-20261115-170213-d2c2131, and read the trajectory files with your own reader. Take the trajmet record layout from athenak/src/particles/, not from docs/FORMATS.md, which is known to be out of date.\n\nV2. D-pre-3 in AthenaK's Newtonian mode. Runs: N128c D-20261115-171503-4262f03, N64c -171505-62940f4, N128Lc -171507-d1058a9; analysis -190541-e27453d. Claims:\n- The turnaround mass and the dress at a/a_i = 2, 4, 8 (the table in secondary_infall/README.md, section 'Wave 2') agree to 0.1-0.5 per cent with a shell reference that uses the measured mesh kernel.\n- The density profile is within 25 per cent of the seeded self-similar solution on lambda = r/r_ta in [0.1, 0.3] at a/a_i = 8.\nMethod: recompute the masses from the particle snapshots with your own definitions of turnaround and dress, written down. Compute the self-similar profile with your own integration, as defined in SCOPE.md. Compare with secondary_infall/selfsimilar.py only after you have your own result.\n\nV3. D-pre-2, Kerr spike reference (wave 2). Run D-bh-dress-20261115-171615-8adbbdd. Claims: spike/kerr_lib.py against Ferrer, da Rosa and Will (arXiv:1707.06302):\n- constant f at a = 0.5 and 0.8 within 0.88 and 0.95 per cent;\n- Hernquist within 1.4-1.5 per cent at a = 0 and on the axis, but 4 per cent below FdRW at the a = 0.8 equatorial peak.\nMethod: write your own action matching, at least for the a = 0.8 equatorial Hernquist case, and say whether the 4 per cent difference lies in the reference, in FdRW or in the comparison.\n\nV4. AthenaK stationarity in Kerr a = 0.8. Run D-bh-dress-20261115-172611-1e40191; analysis -174954-786ddcc. Claims, for 48000 particles over 20000 M:\n- the late/early density ratio is 0.998-1.003;\n- the invariants are conserved to 1e-5;\n- the inner-range time averages lie 1-4 per cent below the reference, all with the same sign.\nMethod: recompute from the snapshots.\n\nV5. The Supplemental Material. Recompute every number of the note's numerical ledger at the pinned commit (note/tables/ledger.tex, generated from claims.json) from the outputs of the run it names. Where an independent recomputation would take hours, rerun the registered analysis instead and mark the row 'rerun, not independent'.\n\nV6. Only if time remains: the wave-1 baselines.\n- Schwarzschild spike (runs D-bh-dress-20261115-123029-4df1e76, -145636-5259f48): peak 0.8699e8 GeV/cm^3 at 7.58 Gm; ratio 2.59 over Gondolo-Silk; +9.2 per cent when the edge moves from 8 to 4 Gm.\n- D-pre-4 drift from 50 to 490 M (runs -121313-284ec4f, -121314-284ec4f): +2.95e-4 at M/8, +3.67e-5 at M/16.\n\nHOW:\n- One registered analysis run per claim group: harness/bin/nrpic-run submit --kind scouting --gate G1 --package tracks/D-bh-dress/verifier_g1 --cores 4 --purpose '...' -- python3 tracks/D-bh-dress/verifier_g1/<script>.py ... Scripts read $NRPIC_RUN_DIR.\n- Before each run, write in verifier_g1/JOURNAL.md what you expect and what would make the claim WRONG.\n- Figures in figstyle (copy harness/style/figstyle.py into your directory). Look at every PNG with the Read tool.\n- Change nothing outside verifier_g1/ and tracks/D-bh-dress/runs/.\n- Commit path-limited: git add tracks/D-bh-dress/verifier_g1 tracks/D-bh-dress/runs, then git commit -m '...' -- those paths.\n- Check the pause flag /data/haiyangw/nrpic/locks/PAUSE before each step.\n\nLIMITS: card time 0. At most 6 processor cores in total; look at uptime first.\n\nDONE WHEN: VERIFIER.md holds a verdict with evidence for each of V1 to V5 (V6 if time allows) and was committed before you read any review; README.md lists your runs and how to rerun them.",
